Cell[TextData[{
 "Some Mathematica versions, for example, version 10.0, 13.3.0,  complains \
about shadowed symbols (check by evaluation  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Names", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Global`\"\>", "<>", "\<\"*\"\>"}], "]"}]], "Input",
  ExpressionUUID->"ebc75168-d719-4ed9-98d2-59dc2563aa57"],
 " in fresh kernel). It is ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " bug, avoid that versions or simply try to delete these symbols when \
checking in very end of section  \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Closing package\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote].  An example is given for ",
 Cell[BoxData["\<\"13.3.1 for Linux x86 (64-bit) (July 24, 2023)\"\>"], 
  "Output",ExpressionUUID->"750b7751-e178-4f09-a22b-29784d1b0b51"],
 "where symbol \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]next\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] is \
removed. Unfortunately, not clear global context of a fresh Mathematica \
session  became a  standard issue in all latest versions of kernel or wolfram \
paclets."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"5490505c-9c07-4cd6-a811-08be9427dba7"],

Cell["\<\
You have to wait until evaluation of this notebook is finished and only then \
evaluate other cells in your notebook. If you press shift + enter on next \
evaluation cell while package load has not been finished for some unknown \
reasons the evaluation of marked cell can be ignored, i.e. simply not sent to \
kernel (you have to reevaluate it after package was loaded). The reason \
remains unclear (front end and OS related bug? some internal evaluation delay \
time limit exceeded?). \
\>", "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"65d3d9d4-4423-4187-9e4e-a793645ae12e"]
}, Closed]]
}, Open  ]],

