}], "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"f6a096a7-1425-4c6f-8d23-dbbea21e4ac5"],

Cell["\<\
1. If some particular function needs to be used before its actual definition \
is given we include its name in declarations of Forwards section. 
2. Options, messages are defined along with the definitions of command. \
Exception are some universal names: Message[gaVerify::obsolete,1,2], etc.
3. Context switch commands are used in Sections.
4. Most of command names are in singular form (i.e. gaIndexList[ ]).  
5. For option names we use Strings. Exceptions are options that are present \
in Mathematica system. In particular we use MaxIterations, Quiet, Method, \
GeneratedParameters, ... names.   This decision has a drawback, that \
options-strings are not visible (no name suggestions when typing, etc). Good \
thing it is that it reduces number of symbol names.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ba37dffc-0dc2-404e-ac1e-fc8db397ae3b"]
}, Closed]],

